# UNERA Mobile App Design Rules

> These rules govern all mobile UI/UX work for the UNERA iOS and Android app. They are grounded in Apple Human Interface Guidelines (HIG), Android Material Design 3 (MD3), and design patterns from leading fintech/crypto apps (Coinbase, Revolut, Cash App, Wise). Every mobile screen, component, and interaction must comply.

---

## 1. Platform Compliance

### iOS — Apple Human Interface Guidelines

- **Navigation**: Use `UITabBarController`-style bottom tab bar as the primary navigation pattern. 3–5 tabs maximum. UNERA uses exactly 5: Home, Wallet, Move, Impact, Profile.
- **Safe areas**: Every screen MUST use `useSafeAreaInsets()` or `<SafeAreaView>`. Account for Dynamic Island (top) and home indicator bar (bottom). Never position interactive elements behind these.
- **Back navigation**: Swipe-from-left-edge must work on every pushed screen. Never disable the system back gesture.
- **Sheet modals**: Transactional flows (Send, Add Money, Exchange, Donate) open as bottom sheets with a drag handle bar, swipe-down to dismiss. Full-screen modals for auth and KYC only.
- **SF Symbols**: Use SF Symbols for system icons (chevron.right, checkmark.circle, qrcode, person.crop.circle, bell, gear, arrow.up, arrow.down) alongside UNERA brand icons.
- **Dynamic Type**: All text must scale with the user's system font size setting. Test at iOS maximum Accessibility text size. Never hardcode fixed-height text containers.
- **Tab bar badges**: Use red oval badges on Home and Profile tabs for unread notification count. Clear on screen visit.
- **Haptics**: Use `expo-haptics` — `Haptics.impactAsync(ImpactFeedbackStyle.Medium)` on success; `ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light` on tap; `Haptics.notificationAsync(NotificationFeedbackType.Error)` on errors.
- **Apple Sign In**: Required on iOS if any social login is offered. Apple Sign In button must appear first (above Google).
- **Screenshot protection**: Apply `FLAG_SECURE` equivalent (`expo-screen-capture` preventScreenCapture) on: seed phrase screens, CVV displays, and wallet address reveals.
- **App Clips**: The "Receive Money" QR entry point should support App Clips for users without the full app installed.

### Android — Material Design 3

- **Navigation**: Use `NavigationBar` (MD3) as the primary bottom navigation. 3–5 destinations. Same 5-tab structure as iOS.
- **Edge-to-edge**: All screens must implement edge-to-edge layout. Handle `WindowInsets` for status bar, navigation bar, and IME (keyboard) properly. Never clip content behind system bars.
- **Predictive back**: Register `onBackInvokedCallback` (Android 14+) for proper predictive back animation support on all screens.
- **Dynamic Color override**: Android 12+ Material You dynamic color MUST be overridden with UNERA brand tokens. Set `colorPrimary: #10B981`, `colorSecondary: #0EA5E9`. Never let wallpaper colors bleed into UNERA UI.
- **Material Symbols**: Use Material Symbols (outlined style) for system icons. Supplement with UNERA brand SVG icons.
- **Adaptive icons**: App icon must use foreground + background layer format for Android home screen. Foreground: UNERA logomark. Background: primary green `#10B981`.
- **Biometrics**: Use `BiometricPrompt` API for all biometric auth — supports fingerprint, face, iris unified. Always check availability and provide password fallback.
- **Haptics**: More limited than iOS. Use `HapticFeedbackConstants.CONFIRM` for success, `REJECT` for errors, `CLOCK_TICK` for selection changes.
- **FCM**: Firebase Cloud Messaging for all push notifications. Create notification channels (`NotificationChannel`) for: Transactions, Impact Updates, Security Alerts, Promotions.
- **Widgets**: Phase 2 — use Jetpack Glance API. Home screen widget shows live balance + quick Send/Receive buttons.

