## 5. Touch Targets & Spacing

- **Minimum touch target: 44×44pt (iOS) / 48×48dp (Android)** — non-negotiable for every interactive element
- **Bottom tab bar items**: min height 49pt (iOS standard) / 56dp (Android MD3 standard)
- **Primary CTA buttons**: `minHeight: 52`, `borderRadius: radius.lg (16)`, full width in sheet modals
- **Secondary buttons**: `minHeight: 48`, outline style
- **Icon-only buttons**: Must be wrapped in a pressable with min 44×44pt hit area even if the icon is smaller
- **List rows**: min height 56pt/dp — use `minHeight: 56` in StyleSheet
- **Spacing between touch targets**: min 8pt gap to prevent accidental taps
- **Form inputs**: `minHeight: 52`, `paddingHorizontal: 16`, `fontSize: 16` (mandatory)

---

## 6. Color Application on Mobile

### Dark Gradient Headers (Trust Pattern)

Portfolio balance screens and primary money displays use the `--gradient-primary` (green → blue) as the screen header background. White text on gradient. This is the signature UNERA mobile pattern — do not replace with a white header for financial data screens.

```
HomeScreen header:    gradient-primary (green → blue), white text
WalletScreen header:  gradient-primary, white text
CentreDetailScreen:   hero image with gradient overlay
Auth screens:         white background (trust + cleanliness)
Sheet modals:         white background
```

### Status Bar

- Over gradient headers: `light-content` (white icons/time)
- Over white backgrounds: `dark-content` (dark icons/time)
- Set programmatically per screen using `expo-status-bar`

### Card Styling on Mobile

```typescript
// Native card — shadow instead of border-only (reads better on native)
const cardStyle = {
  backgroundColor: colors.neutral50,     // white
  borderRadius: radius.xl,               // 20pt — matches web 1.25rem
  // iOS shadow
  shadowColor: '#000',
  shadowOffset: { width: 0, height: 2 },
  shadowOpacity: 0.06,
  shadowRadius: 8,
  // Android elevation
  elevation: 3,
  // Subtle border (keep for consistency with web design)
  borderWidth: 1,
  borderColor: colors.borderSubtle,
};
```

### Do Not Use on Mobile

- ❌ Hardcoded hex values — always reference `theme.ts`
- ❌ `#10B981` (primaryGreen) as text color on white — fails WCAG AA contrast
- ❌ White text on `#10B981` background for body text — use only for large bold text (≥ 18pt bold or ≥ 24pt regular)
- ❌ Custom colors not in the token set — extend `theme.ts` if genuinely needed, document why

