## 7. Security UX

Security is the most critical trust dimension in a fintech app. These rules are non-negotiable.

### Biometric Authentication
- **Biometric is the primary login CTA** — large prominent button ("Use Face ID" / "Use Touch ID" / "Use Fingerprint")
- Auto-trigger biometric prompt on app foreground after session timeout (5 min background)
- Always provide a fallback: "Use Password" link below biometric button
- Show a blurred/masked version of the dashboard behind the lock screen (teases value, motivates unlock)
- Never store auth tokens in AsyncStorage — use `expo-secure-store` (iOS Keychain / Android Keystore)

### Balance & Sensitive Data Masking
- **All balances masked by default** — show "••••••" until user taps to reveal
- Reveal gesture: single tap — do not require hold or swipe
- Re-mask after 30 seconds of inactivity (configurable in settings)
- Masked state: display masked placeholder at same dimensions as the real value (prevents layout shift on reveal)
- Wallet addresses: show first 6 + "…" + last 4 characters. "Show full" button available.

### Transaction Confirmation
- All transactions (Send, Exchange, Withdraw, Stake) require a **Review screen** before confirmation
- Review screen must display: From, To, Amount, Fee, Total deducted — no hidden costs
- For amounts > $50 (configurable): trigger biometric re-authentication before proceeding
- Irreversible actions (seed phrase delete, account delete, large withdrawals): show explicit warning text + require typing "CONFIRM" or similar
- Confirmation button: never auto-enabled — user must scroll to bottom of review details first

### Session Management
- Auto-lock after 5 minutes in background
- Do not show sensitive data in iOS app switcher / Android recent apps — apply `FLAG_SECURE` / blank overlay on `applicationWillResignActive`
- Session timeout banner: "Your session has expired. Tap to unlock." — non-dismissible until biometric/PIN

### KYC & Identity
- Document scan: native camera in portrait mode; no landscape for document scanning
- Selfie: front camera with liveness guidance overlay ("Blink", "Turn left")
- Never store raw document images on device after upload — clear from memory immediately
- Progress is saved server-side: user can resume KYC after app close

