## 8. Accessibility

### VoiceOver (iOS) / TalkBack (Android) — Required

Every interactive element MUST have:
```typescript
// Required on every touchable element
accessibilityLabel="Send money to a contact or address"    // What it is
accessibilityHint="Opens the send money flow"              // What happens
accessibilityRole="button"                                 // Role
```

Rules:
- Decorative images: `accessible={false}` + `importantForAccessibility="no"`
- Amount displays: read as "balance is [amount] dollars, tap to reveal"
- Transaction rows: read full row — "Sent 50 dollars to Alice, March 14, completed"
- Sheet modals: set `accessibilityViewIsModal={true}` to trap focus inside
- Error messages: `accessibilityLiveRegion="assertive"` so screen readers announce immediately
- Loading states: `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"` + "Loading transactions" label

### Dynamic Type / Font Scaling
- All text uses React Native's default `fontSize` in `sp` — scales automatically
- Test every screen at iOS Settings → Accessibility → Display & Text Size → Larger Text (maximum 5 steps)
- `flexWrap: 'wrap'` on all text containers; `numberOfLines` only on non-critical secondary text
- Bottom tab labels must remain visible at large sizes — allow label wrap or abbreviate

### Color Contrast (WCAG AA Minimum)
| Element | Foreground | Background | Ratio | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Primary body text | `#0F172A` | `#FFFFFF` | 19.6:1 | AAA |
| Secondary text | `#475569` | `#FFFFFF` | 6.0:1 | AA |
| White on gradient | `#FFFFFF` | `#10B981` | 2.8:1 | ❌ text only — use bold ≥18pt |
| White on gradient | `#FFFFFF` | `#0EA5E9` | 3.1:1 | ❌ text only — use bold ≥18pt |
| Error text | `#EF4444` | `#FFFFFF` | 4.5:1 | AA ✓ |
| Success text | `#059669` | `#FFFFFF` | 4.6:1 | AA ✓ |

- Rule: white text on the primary gradient is acceptable for **hero balance displays** (large, bold) and **CTA button labels** (bold), NOT for body text or captions.

### Reduced Motion
```typescript
import { useReducedMotion } from 'react-native-reanimated';

const reduceMotion = useReducedMotion();

// Wrap all animations
withTiming(targetValue, {
  duration: reduceMotion ? 0 : 300,
});
```
- When reduced motion is enabled: all transitions are instant (0ms duration)
- Skeleton shimmers: replace with static gray placeholder
- Tab transitions: already instant — no change needed
- Success animations: show static checkmark instead of animated

