## 10. Forms & Input Patterns

### Amount Inputs
- Amount entry for Send, Add Money, Exchange, Donate: use **custom large numpad**, not the system keyboard
- Numpad layout: 3×4 grid (1-9, ., 0, delete); keys min 64×64pt; large font (28pt)
- Live currency conversion: show crypto ↔ fiat toggle instantly as user types
- Maximum amount validation: real-time, inline below input ("Exceeds available balance")
- Leading zeros: strip automatically. "0.50" → "$0.50". Never show "050".
- Decimal: allow one decimal point only; max 2 decimal places for fiat, up to 8 for crypto

### Text Inputs
- Height: `minHeight: 52`, `paddingHorizontal: 16`, `paddingVertical: 14`
- Font size: **16pt minimum** — prevents iOS keyboard zoom on focus
- Border: `borderWidth: 1.5, borderColor: colors.borderSubtle` default; `borderColor: colors.primaryGreen` on focus; `borderColor: colors.error` on validation error
- Labels: above the input, `caption` size, `textSecondary` color, 4pt gap below label
- Error messages: below the input, `caption` size, `colors.error`, shown immediately on blur (not on submit)
- Password fields: always include show/hide toggle (eye icon, right side of input). Use SF Symbol `eye` / `eye.slash` (iOS) or equivalent Material Symbol (Android)
- Placeholder text: `neutral500` color, same font size as input text

### Real-Time Validation
- Validate on field blur (not on keystroke, not on submit)
- Exception: amount fields — validate on keystroke to show balance warnings live
- Error states: red border + error message below field + error icon in field right
- Success states: green border + checkmark icon on fields where confirmation matters (email, username, address)
- Never show a generic "Form has errors" banner — always point to the specific field

### QR Scanner
- Full-screen camera view with scan region overlay (white rounded square frame, 240×240pt)
- Corner markers on scan region (UNERA green, 2pt stroke, 20pt length)
- Status text below frame: "Align QR code within the frame"
- Auto-detect and auto-fill: on QR detection, close camera and populate address field immediately
- Torch/flashlight toggle button in top-right corner
- Manual entry fallback: "Enter address manually" link below camera view

