## 12. Push Notifications

### Notification Categories

Define exactly four channels / categories:

| Category | Channel Name | Examples | Default |
|---|---|---|---|
| `transactions` | Transaction Updates | "You sent $25 to Alice", "You received $100 USDC" | On |
| `impact` | Impact & Centres | "Toronto Centre needs funding", "Your donation funded 3 days" | On |
| `security` | Security Alerts | "New device login", "Password changed", "New session" | On (forced) |
| `marketing` | News & Updates | "New feature: Staking is live", "UNERA monthly report" | Off by default |

### Notification Design Rules
- **Title**: Action verb + subject — "Sent $25.00 to Alice Chen"
- **Body**: Context + outcome — "Transaction confirmed. View receipt →"
- **Never**: "You have a new notification" (useless); price spam; guilt-based re-engagement
- **Rich notifications** (iOS 15+ / Android): include app icon + sender avatar for P2P; include centre image for Impact notifications
- **Grouping**: Group notifications by category in the notification center — not one-by-one
- **Deep link**: Every notification must deep-link to the relevant screen (`unera://transaction/[txId]`, `unera://centre/[centreId]`)
- **Security notifications**: Cannot be disabled by user. Always delivered. No batching.

