## 15. What NOT to Do on Mobile

- ❌ **No hamburger menu** — bottom tab bar only for core navigation
- ❌ **No top navigation bar for the main app** — reserved for screen titles within stacks only
- ❌ **No full-screen loading spinners** — use skeleton shimmers
- ❌ **No modal on top of modal** — maximum 1 modal layer at a time
- ❌ **No auto-playing video or audio** — fintech apps require user consent for media
- ❌ **No gesture conflicts** — swipe-from-edge for back must never conflict with swipe-in-component
- ❌ **No font below 12pt** — ever
- ❌ **No hardcoded hex values** in component files — always reference `theme.ts`
- ❌ **No AsyncStorage for sensitive data** — always `expo-secure-store`
- ❌ **No disabled states without explanation** — if a button is disabled, show why inline
- ❌ **No landscape-locked screens** — all screens must support both orientations (except camera flows)
- ❌ **No Internet Explorer / web-only patterns** — no hover states, no right-click menus, no tooltips on tap (use accessible hints instead)
- ❌ **No launch screen longer than 2 seconds** — splash screen is brand moment only, not a loading gate
- ❌ **No skipping platform review guidelines** — App Store and Google Play rejections cost weeks; comply from the start

