## 16. Icons, Illustrations & Media

> **Source of truth**: All brand/content icons, illustrations, and photography must match the web app reference pages exactly. The web app uses zero external icon libraries — every non-system icon is a handcrafted inline SVG.

---

### 16.0 Design Decisions (Rationale)

These decisions were made to align mobile with web while respecting platform guidelines:

**Emoji replacement** — The web app uses emojis as icons in several places (e.g. 💚 🌍 📈 🔒 🦊 on dashboard, wallet, account-settings). On mobile, emojis are rendered by the OS and look different across Android/iOS versions. **Decision**: Replace emojis with proper inline SVG icons in brand colors (mobile best practice).

**Icon system split** — The existing mobile rule specifies SF Symbols for iOS and Material Symbols for Android for system UI icons (back arrows, chevrons, tab bar icons, eye/hide toggles). The web app uses custom handcrafted inline SVGs for everything — no icon library. **Decision**: Split — system/platform icons (back, chevron, eye, close × , check) stay as SF Symbols / Material Symbols, while BRAND and CONTENT icons (logo, wallet providers, centre illustrations, action icons) match the web SVGs exactly.

