### 16.11 User Avatars

No external avatar service (no Gravatar, no DiceBear, no UI Avatars). User avatars render as styled `<View>` showing the user's initials — same pattern as the web's CSS text-initials `<div>`:

```typescript
// Avatar component pattern
const avatarStyle = {
  width: 40,
  height: 40,
  borderRadius: 20,
  background: gradients.primary, // LinearGradient green→blue
  alignItems: 'center',
  justifyContent: 'center',
};
// Text: user initials (e.g. "JS"), color white, fontSize 14, fontWeight '600'
```

When a user uploads a profile photo, display the photo inside the same circular container with `borderRadius: 9999`.

